<title>UK: Mears Group shares marked higher in AIM debut.</title>
<headline>Mears Group shares marked higher in AIM debut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Mears Group Plc made a firm debut in London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market (AIM) on Friday, trading at 11-1/4p by 1214 GMT, a premium of 12.5 percent on the 10p placing price.</p>
<p>The flotation, sponsored by Apax and Partners, valued Mears at 3.6 million stg and raised 935,000 stg which will go to fund investment and future growth.</p>
<p>The group, based in Berkeley, Gloucestershire, provides response maintenance services to local authorities in southern England and Wales.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
</text>
